[0;30m  [1m∞∞‹€‹€‹€€‹ﬂ‹ﬂ[0m[50C[1;30mﬂ‹ﬂ‹€€‹€‹€‹∞∞
±≤≤›≤›ﬂ[0m[66C[1;30mﬂﬁ≤ﬁ≤≤± €›ﬁﬂ[0m [1;32m   [0m[66C[1;30mﬂ›ﬁ€
‹ﬂ‹[0m[11C[32m10 PRINT[1m [0;32m"[1mPerched nimbly before my old BASIC interpreter,[0m[6C[1;30m‹ﬂ‹€±€[0m[11C[1;32mhome to so many spaghetti codes circular,[0m[22C[1;30m€±€€±€[32m  [0m[64C[1;32m  [0m[6C[1;30m€±€‹ﬂ‹[32m  [0m[9C[1;32mI found myself entering into my keyboard[0m[23C[1;30m‹ﬂ‹€∞€[32m  [0m[9C[1;32msome old type-in listings unknown and unexplored.  [0m[12C[1;30m€∞€€∞€[0m[74C[1;30m€∞€‹€‹[0m [1;32m [0m[9C[1;32mWhat wisdom of gurus and hackers was hidden[0m[20C[1;30m‹€‹€ﬂ€[0m [1;32m [0m[9C[1;32mwithin? As I typed, I stirred up thoughts unbidden  [0m[11C[1;30m€ﬂ€‹ﬂ‹[0m [1;32m [0m[9C[1;32m    [0m[59C[1;30m‹ﬂ‹€€€[0m [1;32m [0m[9C[1;32mof power untold earned through mass calculations,  [0m[12C[1;30m€€€≤€≤[0m [1;32m [0m[9C[1;32mof sinister schemings and foul machinations,[0m[19C[1;30m≤€≤ﬂ‹ﬂ[0m [1;32m [0m[72C[1;30mﬂ‹ﬂ€≤€[0m [1;32m [0m[9C[1;32mof wheels within wheels in a dark subroutine...[0m[16C[1;30m€≤€€≤€[0m [1;32m [0m[9C[1;32mI was finding myself being drawn through the screen! [0m[10C[1;30m€≤€‹ﬂ‹[0m [1;32m [0m[9C[1;32m  [0m[61C[1;30m‹ﬂ‹€±€[0m [1;32m [0m[9C[1;32mI swam through the data, surfed code like a master,  [0m[10C[1;30m€±€€±€[0m [1;32m [0m[9C[1;32mthen found I was bound by the lines of the raster    [0m[10C[1;30m€±€‹ﬂ‹[32m  [0m[72C[1;30m‹ﬂ‹€∞€[32m  [0m[9C[1;32mimprisoning me like the bars of a cage![0m[24C[1;30m€∞€€∞€[32m  [0m[9C[1;32mI tore through the listings exploding with rage.   [0m[12C[1;30m€∞€‹€‹[0m[74C[1;30m‹€‹€ﬂ€[32m  [0m[9C[1;32mBut what had I done?  This was not what I wanted:[0m[14C[1;30m€ﬂ€‹ﬂ‹[32m  [0m[9C[1;32mthe comments suggested this program was haunted! [0m[14C[1;30m‹ﬂ‹€±€[0m[74C[1;30m€±€€±€[32m  [0m[9C[1;32mEscape from this Hell without END I attempted    [0m[14C[1;30m€±€‹ﬂ‹[32m  [0m[9C[1;32mbut every egress was a GOSUB demented[0m[26C[1;30m‹ﬂ‹€∞€[32m  [0m[72C[1;30m€∞€€∞€[32m  [0m[9C[1;32mdiverting the user's aborting the program.[0m[21C[1;30m€∞€‹€‹[32m  [0m[9C[1;32mI'm needing your help to emerge from this logjam.[0m[14C[1;30m‹€‹€ﬂ€[32m  [0m[72C[1;30m€ﬂ€‹ﬂ‹[0m [1;32m [0m[9C[1;32mPlease free me from my IF-THEN-ELSE-ing tormentor[0m[14C[1;30m‹ﬂ‹€€€[0m [1;32m [0m[9C[1;32mI urge you, the user, to mistype and enter[0m[21C[1;30m€€€≤€≤[0m [1;32m [0m[55C[1;32m   [0m[14C[1;30m≤€≤ﬂ‹ﬂ[0m [1;32m [0m[9C[1;32man invalid input - only SYNTAX ERROR[0m[27C[1;30mﬂ‹ﬂ€≤€[0m [1;32m [0m[9C[1;32mcan spare me this limbo of torment and terror... [0m[14C[1;30m€≤€€≤€[0m [1;32m [0m[9C[1;32m   [0m[60C[1;30m€≤€‹ﬂ‹[0m[11C[1;32mand never again will I henpeck in listings -[0m[19C[1;30m‹ﬂ‹€±€[0m[11C[1;32mfree software provided by accursäd [36mMistigris[32m.[0;32m"[1m   [0m[14C[1;30m€±€€±€[0m[11C[32m20 GOTO 10 [37m[36C[1;32m  [0m[14C[1;30m€±€‹ﬂ‹[0m[74C[1;30m‹ﬂ‹€∞€ [0mZombie-like, it arose from its grave after [1;30mcrumbling away in the dank[0m    [1;30m€≤€€∞€ darkness[0m for some sixteen years.  After giving you an unimaginable [1mshock[0m [1;30m€≤€‹ﬂ‹ [0mof recognition across the long and distant ages, it shambled away again, [1;30m‹ﬂ‹€±€ [0mseemingly forever, only to trouble you again a year later.  That was[5C[1;30m€±€€±€ [0mmanageable; you had time to board up the windows, call a priest and[6C[1;30m€±€‹ﬂ‹ [0mprepare yourself.  But last year was different: arriving where you live, [1;30m‹ﬂ‹€∞€ [0mit refused to go away.  Seating itself at your table, the uninvited[6C[1;30m€∞€€∞€ [0mhouseguest demanded to sup on a regular basis until you ran out of ways  [1;30m€∞€‹€‹ [0mto cook brains.  Month in and month out, Mistigris was a constant[8C[1;30m‹€‹€ﬂ€ [0mcompanion[1;30m, not entirely dissimilarly to the parasitic twin celebrated [0m   [1;30m€ﬂ€‹ﬂ‹ in a certain '90s episode of the locally-filmed X-Files television [0m[6C[1;30m‹ﬂ‹€€€ program. [0m[64C[1;30m€€€≤€≤[0m[74C[1;30m≤€≤ﬂ‹ﬂ [37mBut I digress. [0m[58C[1;30mﬂ‹ﬂ€≤€[0m[74C[1;30m€≤€€≤€ [0mThis artist's calendar pretty much revolves around the core holidays of  [1;30m€≤€‹ﬂ‹ [31mHallowe'en[0m and, of course, [35mApril Fool's[37m.  It's not about the scares, but [1;30m‹ﬂ‹€±€ [0mrather the palimpsest practice of the masquerade that appeals.  It was   [1;30m€±€€±€ [0mnot due to proximity to this holiday that we chose October for our first [1;30m€±€‹ﬂ‹ [0mrelease -- that was just how long it took us to get it together after    [1;30m‹ﬂ‹€∞€ [0mhitting the ground running in August 1994 after [1mi[0mMPER[1mi[0mAL folded.  For our[1;30m€∞€€∞€ [0mfirst couple of years the seasonal occasion was barely reflected in our  [1;30m€∞€‹€‹ [0mOctober artpacks, but by the time we got to 1997, thrills and chills were[1;30m‹€‹€ﬂ€ [0mclearly constituting most of the items on the menu.  Fast forward past   [1;30m€ﬂ€‹ﬂ‹ [0mour long [31mliving death[37m and when we returned in 2014, it only made sense to[1;30m‹ﬂ‹€€€ [0mcelebrate the anniversary of our establishment in the month of our first [1;30m€€€≤€≤ [0martpack release.  In 2015 it was apparent that our anniversary artpack   [1;30m≤€≤ﬂ‹ﬂ [0mcontained a smaller Hallowe'en artpack inside of it trying to break free [1;30mﬂ‹ﬂ€≤€ [0m([1;30mI looked it up, the episode's name was [0m"Humbug", [1;30mS02E20[0m), and in 2016 we[1;30m€≤€€≤€ [0mmade it official: reserve October for the scary stuff, and celebrate the [1;30m€≤€‹ﬂ‹ [0manniversary in November.[49C[1;30m‹ﬂ‹€±€[0m[74C[1;30m€±€€±€ [0mSo what does a Hallowe'en-themed artpack after a year of monthly artpack [1;30m€±€‹ﬂ‹ [0mreleases mean on the ground?  It means we've been skimming [1mscary cream[0m   [1;30m‹ﬂ‹€∞€ [0moff the top for a whole year, and dang but that amounts to a veritable   [1;30m€∞€€∞€ [0mmonument of [31mgrand guignol[37m.[47C[1;30m€∞€‹€‹[0m[74C[1;30m‹€‹€ﬂ€ [0mAs we've completed an entire year of monthly artpack releases I've[7C[1;30m€ﬂ€‹ﬂ‹ [0mcrunched some numbers into spreadsheets and uncovered some curious[7C[1;30m‹ﬂ‹€€€ [0mtrends, but probably I should save them for next month's infofile:[7C[1;30m€€€≤€≤ [0mnothing is scarier than the taxman, but he invokes a kind of [1;30mcreeping [0m   [1;30m≤€≤ﬂ‹ﬂ dread[0m rather than evoking terror.  But here's a cool number: [1;33m256[0m.  It's  [1;30mﬂ‹ﬂ€≤€ [0mof significance to mathematicians and computer scientists.  If you don't [1;30m€≤€€≤€ [0mknow why, look up the number's delightful entry on Wikipedia or check out[1;30m€≤€‹ﬂ‹ [0m256stuff.com/256.html ... this heaping collection contains 256 files of  [1;30m‹ﬂ‹€±€ [0mcomputer art for your enjoyment and edification!  Truly no one can say   [1;30m€±€€±€ [0mthat we're not coming by our 8-bit credentials honestly.[17C[1;30m€±€‹ﬂ‹[0m[74C[1;30m‹ﬂ‹€∞€ [0mSo what would be lively news to mention here?  Artists making their[6C[1;30m€∞€€∞€ [0martpack debuts here this month include FANSI artist [1mClear[0m from the[7C[1;30m€∞€‹€‹ [37m8bitMUSH[0m, pixel artists [1mGleeborp [0mand [1mPicture.Elements[0m, "Mr. Hallowe'en"  [1;30m‹€‹€ﬂ€ [0mToren "[1mMacbin[0m" Atkinson and an improbable photograph from [1mMaylee Helene[0m. [1;30m€ﬂ€‹ﬂ‹ [0mNoteworthy or otherwise extraordinary creations in this artpack include: [1;30m‹ﬂ‹€€€ [37mAwesome Angela[0m's foray into [1;36mglow-in-the-dark[0m fusion beads; [1m#inktober[0m[5C[1;30m€€€≤€≤ [0mofferings from various artists, most notably [1mBonemouse[0m;[1m two[0m computer[5C[1;30m≤€≤ﬂ‹ﬂ [0mmusic versions of the same song ([1;30mthe first CD I ever owned, Mike[0m[9C[1;30mﬂ‹ﬂ€≤€ Oldfield's Tubular Bells[0m), arranged by the same musician 25 years apart  [1;30m€≤€€≤€ [0m([1;30mthe ProTracker .MOD of Dorian Grey?[0m); more old ANSI art by [1mSpitoufs[0m on  [1;30m€≤€‹ﬂ‹ [0mhorrific themes, including a comprehensive ANSI-illustrated collection of[1;30m‹ﬂ‹€±€ [0mthe works of [1mEdgar Allan Poe[0m ([1;30mfrom which I poached this infofile's   [0m    [1;30m€±€€±€ framing elements -- though the header logo is by[0m [1mNail[30m, much obliged![0m);   [1;30m€±€‹ﬂ‹ [0mthe return of [1mJ†nos Hor†k[0m with a hilarious pixelart panoramic summoning; [1;30m‹ﬂ‹€∞€ [37mTheresa Oborn[0m back in her native [1;31mspoopy[0m element; and of course a tireless[1;30m€∞€€∞€ [0monslaught of terrifying teletext by [1mHorsenburger[0m.  And I don't know if   [1;30m€∞€‹€‹ [0myou caught this artpack's highlights reel -- I shopped out the standard  [1;30m‹€‹€ﬂ€ [0mpromotional trailer to [1mWasabim[0m, who has demonstrated tremendous[10C[1;30m€ﬂ€‹ﬂ‹ [0mvirtuosity in VFX in his chosen niche of the Atari ST, and he turned[5C[1;30m‹ﬂ‹€€€ [0mour standard pedestrian preview slideshow into a nightmarish gauntlet of [1;30m€€€≤€≤ [0mblood-curdling sights and sounds.  If you haven't yet seen it, I highly  [1;30m≤€≤ﬂ‹ﬂ [0mrecommend you find it on our YouTube channel -- it's an incredible[7C[1;30mﬂ‹ﬂ€≤€ [0menhancement on the artpack's embarrassment of riches.[20C[1;30m€≤€€≤€[0m[74C[1;30m€≤€‹ﬂ‹ [0mAnything else you need to know about?  [1mLord Nikon[0m's exhibit of typewriter[1;30m‹ﬂ‹€±€ [0mart has just wrapped up, but [1mNick Lakowski[0m has just completed a suite of [1;30m€±€€±€ [0mpaintings (which you can view here in this artpack!) for a local[9C[1;30m€±€‹ﬂ‹ [0mexhibition of works inspired by the ancient practice of divination[7C[1;30m‹ﬂ‹€∞€ [0mthrough the examination of entrails -- a neat dovetailing for a painter  [1;30m€∞€€∞€ [0mwhose day job is working as an MRI technician!  I know, you may not think[1;30m€∞€‹€‹ [0mit sounds like the Hallowe'en-iest theme, but when is more appropriate to[1;30m‹€‹€ﬂ€ [0;31munleash a torrent of blood and guts[37m?  For the time being, you can catch  [1;30m€ﬂ€‹ﬂ‹ [0mthe paintings hanging at the [1mAHVA Gallery[0m in room 1001 at the Audain Art [1;30m‹ﬂ‹€€€ [0mCentre in Vancouver's University of British Columbia until November 4th. [1;30m€€€≤€≤[0m[74C[1;30m≤€≤ﬂ‹ﬂ [0mAnd while we're at it, though he might prefer I don't talk about it[6C[1;30mﬂ‹ﬂ€≤€ [0mpublicly ([1;30mdon't worry, I'll hide it away at the end of an infofile where[0m [1;30m€≤€€≤€ we can be well assured that no one will ever see it[0m), I'd like to utter  [1;30m€≤€‹ﬂ‹ [0man unholy [1;31mSamhain[0m prayer for the full recovery of teletext revival[7C[1;30m‹ﬂ‹€±€ [0mvanguard [1mIllarterate[0m, who is presently laid low with horrific health[5C[1;30m€±€€±€ [0mconcerns.[64C[1;30m€±€‹€‹[0m[74C[1;30m‹€‹€ﬂ€ [0mThat said -- let's try to not get our fantasy fright buzz bogged down    [1;30m€ﬂ€‹ﬂ‹‹   [0min "[1;30mthe horror of existence[0m".  Come get your creep on!  We'll catch [1;30m‹ﬂ‹ﬂ‹€∞€ € [0myou again in a month for our fabulous 23rd anniversary extravaganza! [1;30m€ €∞€€∞€ €[0m[70C[1;30m€ €∞€‹€‹ €[0m[7C[1mMistigris 2017:[0m [1mComing by our 8-bit credentials honestly.[0m[6C[1;30m€ ‹€‹€ﬂ€ﬂ‹ﬂ‹[0m[66C[1;30m‹ﬂ‹ﬂ€ﬂ€‹ﬂ‹ﬂ‹ﬂ ‹[0m[64C[1;30m‹ ﬂ‹ﬂ‹ﬂ‹€€€‹ﬂﬂ≤ ‹[0m[20C[1;30m   [0m‹[1m‹[47m‹€€€€€€‹[40m‹[0m‹[1;30m‹ [0m[25C[1;30m‹ ≤ﬂﬂ‹€€€≤€≤€‹ﬂﬂ≤ ‹[0m[19C[1;30m [0m‹[1;47;33m‹€€[37m€[33m€[37m€€€€€€€€≤‹[30mﬂ[40m‹   [0m[19C[1;30m‹ ≤ﬂﬂ‹€≤€≤ﬂ≤≤€€‹ﬂﬂ≤ ‹[0m[18Cﬁ[1;47;33m€€≤≤≤[37m≤≤≤≤≤≤≤€ﬂ[36m∞∞∞[0m€[1;47;30mﬂ[40m‹ [0m[18C[1;30m‹ ≤ﬂﬂ‹€€≤≤ﬂ ±€≤€€‹ﬂﬂ≤ ‹[0m[16C[1;47;30mﬂ[33m‹≤‹∞∞[0m€€[1;47m‹‹[36m∞∞[37m∞∞[0m€[1;47;30m‹[40m€€[0m€[1;47;30m∞∞≤[40m›[0m[17C[1;30m‹ ≤ﬂﬂ‹€€≤€±
